SignatureLib::verifySignatures
├── given init mode (isInit = true)
│   ├── when user signature is valid EOA
│   │   └── it succeeds (skips allocator check)
│   ├── when user signature is valid smart account
│   │   └── it succeeds (skips allocator check)
│   └── when allocator signature is invalid
│       └── it succeeds (allocator not checked in init mode)
├── given non-init mode (isInit = false)
│   ├── when msg.sender is user
│   │   ├── when allocator is smart account with valid signature
│   │   │   └── it succeeds (skips user check)
│   │   └── when allocator is EOA
│   │       └── it reverts
│   ├── when msg.sender is not user
│   │   ├── when both signatures are valid smart accounts
│   │   │   └── it succeeds
│   │   ├── when allocator is EOA and user is smart account
│   │   │   └── it reverts
│   │   ├── when allocator signature is invalid (wrong signer)
│   │   │   └── it reverts with InvalidAllocatorSignature
│   │   ├── when allocator signature is invalid (wrong hash)
│   │   │   └── it reverts with InvalidAllocatorSignature
│   │   ├── when user signature is invalid (wrong signer)
│   │   │   └── it reverts with InvalidUserSignature
│   │   ├── when user signature is invalid (wrong hash)
│   │   │   └── it reverts with InvalidUserSignature
│   │   ├── when allocator signature is malformed
│   │   │   └── it reverts with InvalidAllocatorSignature
│   │   └── when user wallet returns invalid
│   │       └── it reverts with InvalidUserSignature
│   └── when signatures are empty
│       └── it reverts with InvalidUserSignature
└── given allocator is zero address
    └── it skips allocator signature check